# Every endpoint, top to bottom. Needs the VS Code REST Client extension
# (humao.rest-client); start the service first with `docker compose up --build`.
# Request 1 is named, so later requests reuse the created order's ID.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@orderId = {{createOrder.response.body.id}}

### 1. Create a checkout intent → 201 (200 when re-sent with the same body)
# @name createOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "merchant_id": "m_123", "order_reference": "ORD-1001", "amount": 1999, "currency": "EUR" }

### 2. Same reference, different amount → 409, order unchanged
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "merchant_id": "m_123", "order_reference": "ORD-1001", "amount": 2500, "currency": "EUR" }

### 3. Same reference, another merchant → 201, a different order
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "merchant_id": "m_456", "order_reference": "ORD-1001", "amount": 1999, "currency": "EUR" }

### 4. Invalid checkout (lowercase currency, zero amount) → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "merchant_id": "m_123", "order_reference": "ORD-1002", "amount": 0, "currency": "eur" }

### 5. Get the order → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}

### 6. Get a malformed or unknown ID → 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/not-a-uuid

### 7. Webhook: processing → 200, applied
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "event_id": "evt_demo_processing", "order_id": "{{orderId}}", "status": "processing", "occurred_at": "2026-10-06T12:01:00Z" }

### 8. Webhook: succeeded (fixed event_id) → 200, applied. Send it twice: the second is a duplicate, still 200, applied once
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "event_id": "evt_demo_duplicate", "order_id": "{{orderId}}", "status": "succeeded", "occurred_at": "2026-10-06T12:01:30Z" }

### 9. Same event_id, different status → 200, never applied, logged as a conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "event_id": "evt_demo_duplicate", "order_id": "{{orderId}}", "status": "failed", "occurred_at": "2026-10-06T12:01:30Z" }

### 10. Late processing after success → 200, recorded as ignored
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "event_id": "evt_demo_late", "order_id": "{{orderId}}", "status": "processing", "occurred_at": "2026-10-06T12:00:30Z" }

### 11. Malformed webhook (non-UUID order_id) → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "event_id": "evt_demo_bad", "order_id": "not-a-uuid", "status": "succeeded", "occurred_at": "2026-10-06T12:01:30Z" }

### 12. Webhook for an unknown order → 404, logged
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "event_id": "evt_demo_unknown", "order_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000", "status": "succeeded", "occurred_at": "2026-10-06T12:01:30Z" }

### 13. Check the final status → succeeded
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}
